{"type":"npc","name":"Sarcophagus Lid","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":64,"temp":0,"max":64,"details":"void healing"},"ac":{"value":28,"details":"void healing"},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":null,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"fly","value":40}],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"object-immunities","exceptions":[]}],"weaknesses":[],"hardness":{"value":8}},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["necril"],"details":"Plus any one language they knew when they were alive"},"level":{"value":8},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Necromancers seeking resilient mummy guardians developed a ritual for creating mummies capable of using their own sarcophagi for defense, either as a shield to protect the mummy from damage or as an independent minion capable of fighting alongside the mummy. Either way, by fighting in concert with their sarcophagus, a sealed mummy is much more dangerous than a mere mummy guardian.</p><p>While many of the unfortunate individuals who become mummies are unwilling and arise with hatred for all living things, sealed mummies retain their memories and loyalties to those they once served. These mummies tend to be people who chose undeath in order to guard someone or something that inspired their eternal devotion, and they follow their liege or their ward beyond the grave.</p><h2>Unlidded</h2><p>A sealed mummy prizes their sarcophagus lid, which often bears a likeness of themselves as they were in life, above all else. When their sarcophagus lid is broken, a sealed mummy sometimes go berserk with rage, abandoning all other goals beyond seeking revenge on those who defaced their precious lid.</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":6},"dex":{"mod":3},"con":{"mod":4},"int